# Why: everything listed here is EXCLUDED from the Docker build context.
#
# Two reasons this matters:
#   1. Speed — without it, `node_modules/` and `.venv/` (hundreds of MB) are uploaded to
#      the Docker daemon on every single build, even though the image rebuilds them anyway.
#   2. SECURITY — without it, a local `.env` containing real secrets gets baked into an
#      image layer. Layers are immutable and are pushed to a registry. Deleting the file in
#      a later RUN step does NOT remove it from the earlier layer; anyone who can pull the
#      image can extract it. This is a top-10 container security mistake.

.git/
.github/
docs/

**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov/

docker-data/
*.md
!README.md
